{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Therefore I will again add.</b> Like ונשאר אני (Ezekiel 9:8), כי אומלל אני (Psalms 6:3), because it has pataḥ under the lamed, and some say the word יוסיף is a verb on the pattern of תומך גורלי (Psalms 16:5):" "<b>Wonder upon wonder.</b> That they will not understand, therefore after it 'and perished,' and some say it is like עושה פלא (Exodus 15:11), and in my opinion, doing a wonder like this:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The citation תהלים ו' ג' matches Psalms 6:3 in verse numbering; 'pataḥ under the lamed' refers to the form לכן in the lemma."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:51.604731203Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}